# Contributing to {{PROJECT_TITLE}}

This project uses the AI-ready project harness. Contributions, whether
from humans or AI agents, must follow the documented gates.

---

## 1. Before you start

- Read `AGENTS.md` and `CLEAN_STATE_CHECKLIST.md`.
- Open `docs/00-project-control/current-state.yml` to find the active
  task. If you need a new task, follow `bootstrap-project-context` or
  ask the Project Manager.
- Verify you are on the correct branch
  (`current-state.yml.current.active_branch`).

---

## 2. While you work

- Create or update artifacts using the templates under
  `.harness/templates/`.
- Validate structured artifacts against `.harness/schemas/`.
- Keep your changes scoped to the active task. Out-of-scope cleanups
  go into a follow-up task, not the current PR.
- Record open questions in
  `docs/00-project-control/questions/open-question-log.md` rather than
  guessing.

---

## 3. Before you open a PR

Clear the `pre-pr` block of `CLEAN_STATE_CHECKLIST.md`.

The reviewer will run `review-pr` (see `.harness/commands.yml`) which
checks:

- `gates.before_pull_request`
- `quality.documentation`
- `quality.technical`
- `quality.anti_fiction`

---

## 4. End of session

Run `end-session`. Do not leave handoff files stale.

---

## 5. Improving the harness itself

The `{{KIT_ROOT}}/` directory is read-only during normal project work.
Proposals to change harness rules, templates, or workflows go through
`propose-harness-improvement` and require human approval.
